window.LILIAN_STORIES={"ea01u":{"subtitle":{"zh":"让 AI 助手接入日常用车任务","en":"An AI assistant across everyday vehicle tasks"},"lead":{"zh":"在德赛西威 EA01U 团队项目中，我的工作涵盖 AI 座舱研究、任务流程与交互架构，以及界面和交互原型设计。设计围绕桌面（Launcher）卡片编辑、虚拟个人助理（VPA）创作，以及车控、电话和音乐等日常任务展开。","en":"Within Desay SV’s EA01U team, my work includes AI cockpit research, task flows, interaction architecture, UI design and interactive prototyping. The designs cover Launcher card editing, virtual personal assistant (VPA) creation and everyday tasks involving vehicle control, calls and music."},"question":{"zh":"当一句请求涉及多个车辆服务时，界面怎样让用户看清助手正在做什么、下一步能做什么？","en":"When a request spans several vehicle services, how can the interface make the assistant’s actions and the user’s next choices clear?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"梳理请求与服务","en":"Map requests to services"},"description":{"zh":"从用户意图出发，连接模型理解、车辆能力与执行反馈。","en":"Connect user intent, model interpretation, vehicle capabilities and execution feedback."}},{"label":{"zh":"设计助手的可见状态","en":"Make assistant states visible"},"description":{"zh":"研究对话组件、创作入口与人设状态，呈现助手的进度和回应。","en":"Use conversation components, creation states and persona expressions to communicate progress and responses."}},{"label":{"zh":"以日常任务组织原型","en":"Build around everyday tasks"},"description":{"zh":"用卡片编辑与 AI 故事线，展示不同服务如何组成连续体验。","en":"Show card editing and connected services through Launcher prototypes and an everyday AI journey."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[0,1],"title":{"zh":"先看 AI 在座舱中的位置","en":"Start with AI’s place in the cockpit"},"text":{"zh":"Launcher 将导航、服务卡片与 VPA 放在同一桌面。结合官方影片与动态原型，先看清助手与日常用车信息的关系，再进入具体交互。","en":"The Launcher places navigation, service cards and the VPA on one home screen. The official film and motion prototype establish how the assistant sits alongside everyday vehicle information before the case study turns to individual interactions."},"layout":"immersive","detailsLabel":{"zh":"平台背景与 Launcher 桌面布局说明","en":"Platform background and Launcher layout notes"}},{"sections":[2,3,7],"title":{"zh":"把用户请求拆成车辆任务","en":"Translate a request into vehicle tasks"},"text":{"zh":"研究将用户表达、模型理解和车辆服务连成一条任务链。架构图与垂域划分进一步明确：系统如何理解请求，调用哪些能力，以及执行后需要返回什么信息。","en":"The research links a user’s request to model interpretation and vehicle services. The architecture and service-domain map clarify how a request is understood, which capabilities it calls on and what feedback follows an action."},"layout":"system","detailsLabel":{"zh":"请求拆解、系统架构与车辆服务分类","en":"Request analysis, system architecture and vehicle services"}},{"sections":[4,5,6],"title":{"zh":"用界面说明助手在做什么","en":"Show what the assistant is doing"},"text":{"zh":"对话组件回答“系统正在做什么”，界面形态决定“内容在哪里展开”，助手身份则提示“它能提供什么帮助”。三组研究共同支持座舱 AI 的反馈表达。","en":"Conversation components explain what the system is doing; interface patterns determine where content appears; assistant identity communicates the kind of help on offer. These studies shape the visible feedback of the cockpit AI."},"layout":"research","detailsLabel":{"zh":"对话组件、界面形态与助手身份说明","en":"Notes on conversation components, layouts and assistant identity"}},{"sections":[8,9,10],"title":{"zh":"从创作入口到有动作的 VPA","en":"From creation entry to an expressive VPA"},"text":{"zh":"创作流程从初始引导和后台生成反馈开始，延伸到角色创作、动作库与预设动画。这些原型共同说明用户如何获得自己的助手，以及角色如何在桌面中呈现。","en":"The flow moves from initial guidance and generation feedback to character creation, an action library and preset animation. Together, the prototypes show how a user could create an assistant and how that character could appear on the home screen."},"layout":"sequence","detailsLabel":{"zh":"VPA 生成流程与动作设计说明","en":"VPA creation flow and motion-design notes"}},{"sections":[11,12],"title":{"zh":"用卡片与故事线组织日常任务","en":"Organize everyday tasks through cards and a storyline"},"text":{"zh":"卡片编辑处理桌面编排，AI 故事线则连接欢迎、提醒、简报、车控、电话与音乐。两组原型分别展示用户如何调整常用信息，以及服务如何在连续情境中衔接。","en":"Card editing addresses the arrangement of the home screen, while the AI storyline connects welcomes, alerts, briefings, vehicle control, calls and music. The prototypes show both how users could arrange information and how services could connect across a journey."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"卡片编辑与 AI 任务旅程说明","en":"Card editing and AI task-journey notes"}},{"sections":[13,14,15],"title":{"zh":"个性可以不同，状态需要清楚","en":"Vary the persona while keeping states clear"},"text":{"zh":"VPA 广场、人设状态矩阵与自定义流程从三个角度展开个性化：选择谁来对话、理解角色当前的状态，以及调整外观或描述生成需求。","en":"VPA Plaza, the persona-state matrix and the customization flow cover three aspects of personalization: choosing a companion, understanding its current state and shaping its appearance through settings or a description."},"layout":"states","detailsLabel":{"zh":"人设状态与自定义流程说明","en":"Persona states and customization-flow notes"}}],"closing":{"zh":"这项进行中的团队工作，将 AI 座舱研究连接到可观看的界面与动态原型。对我而言，关键是把助手的能力落实到具体任务，并通过入口、状态与执行反馈，让复杂服务的过程更容易被理解。","en":"This ongoing team project connects AI cockpit research with interface and motion prototypes. My focus is on translating assistant capabilities into concrete tasks and making service entry, system state and execution feedback understandable throughout the interaction."}},"aurora-mood":{"subtitle":{"zh":"驾驶信息优先，AI 陪伴由你选择","en":"Driving information first, AI companionship by choice"},"lead":{"zh":"这是一个个人座舱概念项目。我围绕抬头显示（HUD）、中控与 AI 伙伴划分信息优先级，并以拥堵场景、舒适联动和音量手势探索用户如何选择和控制辅助功能。","en":"In this personal cockpit concept, I defined the roles of the HUD, center display and AI companion. A congestion scenario, coordinated comfort settings and a volume gesture explore how optional assistance could enter the driving experience."},"question":{"zh":"怎样让驾驶者持续看清关键信息，同时能够自主选择 AI 陪伴与舒适体验？","en":"How can drivers keep essential information in view while choosing when to use AI companionship and comfort features?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"划分信息优先级","en":"Set information priorities"},"description":{"zh":"将速度、导航与行程放在 HUD，把丰富内容与舒适设置交给中控。","en":"Place speed, navigation and trip information in the HUD, with richer content and comfort settings on the center display."}},{"label":{"zh":"用场景说明交互","en":"Explain interactions through a scenario"},"description":{"zh":"展示拥堵中的建议、用户确认与舒适联动，并提出音量手势概念。","en":"Show a suggestion, confirmation and coordinated comfort settings in traffic, alongside a volume-gesture concept."}},{"label":{"zh":"为下一轮补全边界","en":"Define the next interaction rules"},"description":{"zh":"明确行车与驻车、拒绝退出，以及手势识别不清时的处理方向。","en":"Plan rules for driving and parked modes, decline and exit, and ambiguous gesture input."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[7,6],"title":{"zh":"先看 HUD 与中控如何分工","en":"See how the HUD and center display divide the work"},"text":{"zh":"整体座舱与界面图呈现两个重点：HUD 稳定承接驾驶核心，中控容纳 AI 伙伴、内容与舒适控制。21:9 屏幕和氛围视觉将这些局部设计放回同一空间。","en":"The cockpit mockup and interface views establish two roles: the HUD carries driving essentials, while the center display accommodates the AI companion, content and comfort controls. The 21:9 display and ambient visuals bring these elements into one space."},"layout":"immersive","detailsLabel":{"zh":"HUD、中控与座舱布局说明","en":"HUD, center-display and cockpit layout notes"}},{"sections":[2,3],"title":{"zh":"决定什么要常驻，什么可以展开","en":"Decide what stays visible and what can expand"},"text":{"zh":"我以清晰信息和低压力辅助作为目标体验，将驾驶、拥堵与休息情境对应到不同内容。信息架构据此区分常驻驾驶信息与可选体验内容。","en":"I framed the intended experience around clear information and assistance that makes modest demands on attention. Driving, congestion and rest scenarios inform the division between information that stays visible and optional content that can expand."},"layout":"system","detailsLabel":{"zh":"目标场景与信息架构说明","en":"Scenario and information-architecture notes"}},{"sections":[4,5],"title":{"zh":"把 AI 建议放进可选择的流程","en":"Place AI suggestions within a flow the user can choose"},"text":{"zh":"拥堵流程展示建议、确认与音乐、灯光、座椅的联动；音量光环则探索手势和视觉反馈的对应。两项方案共同追问：辅助如何被开启、被理解，并在需要时被停止。","en":"The congestion flow shows a suggestion, confirmation and coordinated music, lighting and seat settings. The volume ring explores the link between gesture and visual feedback. Both examine how assistance can be started, understood and stopped."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看拥堵联动与音量手势方案","en":"View the congestion flow and volume-gesture concept"}},{"sections":[0,1],"title":{"zh":"用色彩与动态统一座舱语气","en":"Unify the cockpit through color and motion"},"text":{"zh":"视觉方向以深蓝建立空间感，以青色组织信息，并用暖色增加陪伴体验的温度。配色与动态参考围绕同一目标展开：让未来感与平静感同时成立。","en":"Deep blue establishes the spatial setting, cyan organizes information and warm accents give the companion experience a more human tone. Color and motion references develop a futuristic yet calm character for the cockpit."},"layout":"visual","detailsLabel":{"zh":"概念定位与配色依据","en":"Concept direction and color rationale"}},{"sections":[8,9,10],"title":{"zh":"把下一轮原型要验证的规则写清","en":"Define the rules for the next prototype"},"text":{"zh":"视觉方案之后，下一步是把行车与驻车切换、建议的拒绝与退出、手势误操作恢复做成可操作流程。这些规则将用于检查可读性、注意力需求与用户控制感。","en":"The next step is to prototype driving and parked mode changes, decline and exit paths, and recovery from unintended gestures. These rules will guide checks of legibility, attention demands and the user’s control over the experience."},"layout":"rules","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看模式切换、退出与误操作规则","en":"Read the mode, exit and gesture-recovery rules"}}],"closing":{"zh":"项目形成了八组视觉方案、座舱效果图与后续交互规则。它把“有情绪温度的座舱”落实为可讨论的信息分工和场景流程，也明确了下一轮需要重点检查的驾驶可读性与操作恢复。","en":"The project produced eight visual boards, a cockpit mockup and a set of interaction rules for the next iteration. It translates the idea of a more human cockpit into an information architecture and scenario flows, with legibility and recovery as priorities for the next prototype."}},"generative-hmi":{"subtitle":{"zh":"把页面生成纳入可检查的设计流程","en":"Bring screen generation into a reviewable design workflow"},"lead":{"zh":"这一专题围绕生成式 HMI 的应用方案展开。我将风格规则、组件模板、多页面关系和局部修改整理到同一流程，并规划原型评估任务与检查标准。","en":"This study develops an application plan for generative HMI. I organized style rules, component templates, page relationships and local editing into a workflow, together with tasks and review criteria for prototype evaluation."},"question":{"zh":"怎样让生成的 HMI 页面遵循同一套组件与风格，并能按要求修改局部内容？","en":"How can generated HMI screens follow shared components and style rules while supporting a requested local change?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"明确生成输入","en":"Define the generation inputs"},"description":{"zh":"把任务、风格规则、组件结构与页面关系整理成明确输入。","en":"Specify the task, style rules, component structure and page relationships."}},{"label":{"zh":"划定修改范围","en":"Set the scope of an edit"},"description":{"zh":"同时说明目标区域与需要保留的内容，便于检查意外改动。","en":"Identify both the target region and the content to preserve so unintended changes can be checked."}},{"label":{"zh":"安排可比较的评估","en":"Plan a comparable evaluation"},"description":{"zh":"用共同任务与标准，规划多页面生成和局部修改的模型比较。","en":"Use common tasks and criteria to plan model comparisons for multi-page generation and local editing."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[0,1],"title":{"zh":"先定义生成需要知道什么","en":"Define what the generation process needs to know"},"text":{"zh":"应用方案将任务、风格规则和组件模板放在生成之前，并在生成之后安排检查与修改。输入结构的目的，是把“页面应该怎样”转成可以对照的要求。","en":"The application plan places the task, style rules and component templates before generation, followed by review and revision. Structuring the inputs turns expectations for a screen into requirements that can be checked."},"layout":"system","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看生成流程与输入清单","en":"Read the generation workflow and input list"}},{"sections":[2,3],"title":{"zh":"分别检查跨页一致性与局部修改","en":"Check cross-page consistency and local editing separately"},"text":{"zh":"页面生成需要保持共享组件和状态表达；局部修改则需要识别目标，并保留周边关系。我将两类任务分开规划，便于定位生成过程中的不同问题。","en":"Page generation needs consistent shared components and state expression. Local editing needs a defined target and stable surrounding relationships. I planned these as separate tasks to make different types of generation failure easier to identify."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看跨页一致性与局部修改检查项","en":"Read the cross-page and local-edit checks"}},{"sections":[4,5],"title":{"zh":"用原型证据评估这条工作流","en":"Evaluate the workflow through prototype evidence"},"text":{"zh":"后续比较将统一任务、输入和检查标准，记录输出、失败案例与修改过程。结果将用于调整工作流：哪些约束要更明确，哪些环节需要增加检查。","en":"The planned comparison will use common tasks, inputs and criteria and record outputs, failed cases and revisions. The findings will guide changes to the workflow, including constraints that need clarification and steps that need additional review."},"layout":"rules","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看模型比较标准与下一阶段任务","en":"Read the comparison criteria and next-stage tasks"}}],"closing":{"zh":"当前产出是应用工作流、输入结构与原型评估规划。这个过程让我把生成式 HMI 从一次页面输出拆成连续的设计任务：先说明要求，再检查一致性，最后追踪修改是否准确。下一步将用实际原型验证这套流程。","en":"The current outputs are an application workflow, an input structure and a prototype evaluation plan. This work breaks generative HMI into a sequence of design tasks: specify requirements, review consistency and track edit accuracy. The next step is to examine the workflow through a working prototype."}},"the-world-of-kantan":{"subtitle":{"zh":"把休息时的内疚，放进一个细胞世界","en":"A cellular world about guilt, rest and self-worth"},"lead":{"zh":"项目从家人休息时仍觉得自己落后的经历出发，制作了一个发生在细胞内部的 VR 交互原型。角色通过收集细胞器组装身体，而旅程最后的一盆风信子，将注意力从不断积累转向生长与照料。","en":"Inspired by a family member who felt behind even while resting, this VR prototype takes place inside a cellular world. Collecting organelles lets the character assemble a body, while a hyacinth at the end of the journey shifts attention from accumulation to growth and care."},"question":{"zh":"当休息也让人觉得自己不够努力，游戏能如何帮助我们重新看待自我价值？","en":"When even rest feels unproductive, how might a game offer another way to think about self-worth?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"从身边的压力出发","en":"Start with a familiar pressure"},"description":{"zh":"结合家人的经历与生产力内疚研究，确定项目要讨论的感受。","en":"Connect a family member’s experience with research into guilt around productivity."}},{"label":{"zh":"设计角色与收集玩法","en":"Build characters and a collection journey"},"description":{"zh":"用细胞器、向导和敌对细胞核，表现积累、压力与重新开始。","en":"Use organelles, a guide and hostile cell nuclei to explore accumulation, pressure and starting again."}},{"label":{"zh":"把植物带回日常","en":"Take a plant into everyday life"},"description":{"zh":"以带走风信子的结尾设计，让游戏与日后的照料相连。","en":"Connect the game’s ending with an ongoing act of care through a hyacinth to take home."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[2],"title":{"zh":"一个可以进入的细胞世界","en":"Step inside the cellular world"},"text":{"zh":"场景以粉紫色、生物纹理和细胞形态建立柔软而陌生的环境。世界观与 3D 场景把“越积累才越有价值”的压力放到身体之外，让玩家能够通过角色和空间接近这个话题。","en":"Pink and violet colours, biological textures and cellular forms establish a soft, unfamiliar setting. The world-building and 3D scenes place the pressure to keep accumulating outside the self, giving players a character and a landscape through which to approach it."},"layout":"immersive","detailsLabel":{"zh":"细胞世界与场景构成说明","en":"Cellular-world and scene-design notes"}},{"sections":[0],"title":{"zh":"为什么休息时仍会内疚","en":"Why rest can still feel like falling behind"},"text":{"zh":"家人难以安心休息的经历，引出了对生产力内疚与奖励循环的研究。园艺疗愈提供了另一种时间感：植物的生长需要等待和持续照料。因此，风信子既是游戏中的引导意象，也是连接体验与日常生活的物件。","en":"A family member’s difficulty resting prompted research into productivity guilt and reward loops. Horticultural therapy suggested a different pace, centred on waiting and ongoing care. The hyacinth became both a guiding image within the game and an object connecting the proposed experience with everyday life."},"layout":"research","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看压力研究与风信子意象的来源","en":"Read the research behind the pressure and hyacinth imagery"}},{"sections":[1],"title":{"zh":"让角色与玩法表达压力","en":"Express pressure through characters and play"},"text":{"zh":"Kantan 通过收集细胞器组装自己，在向导带领下探索场景，并面对敌对细胞核。角色设定、Blender 模型与交互原型共同呈现这段旅程如何展开。结尾从虚拟收集转向照料真实植物，为整个体验留下一个更缓慢的收尾。","en":"Kantan assembles a body by collecting organelles, follows a guide through the landscape and encounters hostile cell nuclei. Character sheets, Blender models and the interaction prototype show how the journey unfolds. Its ending moves from virtual collection to caring for a real plant, introducing a slower rhythm."},"layout":"sequence","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看角色设定、建模与交互分镜","en":"View character designs, models and interaction storyboards"}}],"closing":{"zh":"项目完成了细胞世界、角色模型与交互原型，将家人的经历发展为一段可以参与的空间叙事。后续希望通过参与者反馈，观察收集与对抗的节奏是否仍在重复项目想讨论的生产力压力，并据此调整体验。","en":"The project produced a cellular environment, character models and an interaction prototype, developing a family experience into a participatory spatial narrative. Further participant feedback could explore whether collection and confrontation repeat the productivity pressure the project questions, and help refine the experience."}},"this-conversation":{"subtitle":{"zh":"让孩子的解释，也能被认真听见","en":"Make room for a young person’s side of the story"},"lead":{"zh":"This Conversation 关注亲子争执中不对等的发言权，提出虚拟小法庭与实体桌游两种对话方式。项目从访谈与旅程梳理出发，设计事件陈述、情绪表达、调解与反馈的流程，让双方有机会把一件事慢慢说清楚。","en":"This Conversation addresses unequal speaking rights in family disagreements through a virtual mini-court and a physical board game. Research and journey mapping inform a sequence of describing events, expressing feelings, mediation and feedback, giving parents and young people a way to work through one disagreement together."},"question":{"zh":"在父母与孩子意见不一致时，怎样让双方都有机会说清自己的感受和理由？","en":"When parents and young people disagree, how can both have space to explain what they feel and why?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"了解为什么难以开口","en":"Understand what makes speaking difficult"},"description":{"zh":"从访谈中整理保护、控制与隐藏感受之间的关系。","en":"Use interviews to examine protection, control and the choice to keep feelings hidden."}},{"label":{"zh":"把争执拆成对话步骤","en":"Break an argument into a conversation"},"description":{"zh":"分别安排事件陈述、调解、外部反馈和共同回顾。","en":"Give event descriptions, mediation, outside feedback and reflection their own stages."}},{"label":{"zh":"用卡牌表达难说的感受","en":"Use cards to express difficult feelings"},"description":{"zh":"通过事件排序、情绪卡和强度标记，支持面对面交流。","en":"Support face-to-face discussion through event sequencing, mood cards and intensity markers."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[3,4],"title":{"zh":"在虚拟空间与桌面上练习对话","en":"Two ways to work through a disagreement"},"text":{"zh":"虚拟小法庭让双方提交冲突，由调解角色引导陈述，并引入访客投票作为外部反馈；实体桌游则把事件和感受放到桌面上，用卡牌与情绪强度标记帮助表达。两种形式都围绕“先说清楚，再听对方”组织流程。","en":"In the virtual mini-court, participants submit a disagreement, explain it with guidance from a mediator and receive outside feedback through visitor voting. The physical game places events and feelings on the table through cards and emotional-intensity markers. Both formats organise the conversation around explaining a perspective and then hearing another."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"数字小法庭与桌游的设计说明","en":"Mini-court and board-game design notes"}},{"sections":[0,1],"title":{"zh":"争执背后，是谁更有资格说话","en":"Who gets to be heard in a family argument?"},"text":{"zh":"访谈材料中，父母常把严格要求视为保护，孩子却可能因为年龄与经验而失去解释的机会。项目因此将设计重点放在发言权：为双方保留描述事件与感受的环节，并用共同参与的场景帮助他们看见彼此的立场。","en":"Interview material describes strict demands being framed as protection, while a young person’s age or experience can limit their chance to explain. This led the design towards speaking rights: reserving space for both accounts and using a shared setting to make each perspective visible."},"layout":"research","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看家庭沟通研究与访谈发现","en":"Read the family-communication research and interview findings"}},{"sections":[2],"title":{"zh":"从各自陈述，到一起回顾","en":"From separate accounts to shared reflection"},"text":{"zh":"旅程地图将体验分为进入、陈述、调解、投票与回顾。场景与界面设计围绕每一步要表达什么、由谁参与，以及接下来会发生什么展开，让一次容易失控的争执有一条可以共同遵循的讨论路径。","en":"The journey map separates arrival, explanation, mediation, voting and reflection. Scenario and interface design clarify what is expressed at each stage, who takes part and what follows, giving a difficult disagreement a sequence that both participants can follow."},"layout":"sequence","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看对话旅程与各阶段的参与方式","en":"Explore the dialogue journey and participation at each stage"}}],"closing":{"zh":"项目形成了家庭对话的服务旅程、虚拟小法庭界面与实体桌游方案，将访谈中难以被听见的感受转为具体的表达工具。后续需要进一步讨论访客权限与投票的呈现方式，避免外部评价给本就难以开口的孩子增加压力。","en":"The project produced a service journey, virtual mini-court interfaces and a physical board-game proposal, turning feelings described in interviews into concrete tools for expression. Further development should examine visitor access and the presentation of voting, so outside judgement does not add pressure for a young person who already finds speaking difficult."}},"meditate-naturally":{"subtitle":{"zh":"用身体信号连接冥想与自然","en":"Connect meditation and nature through bodily signals"},"lead":{"zh":"Meditate Naturally 是一个结合服装、脑波数据与双投影的团队装置，邀请参与者在冥想中重新留意身体与自然。我负责脑波数据解析、TouchDesigner 视觉映射和投影反馈，将输入信号变为服装与背景上的图像变化。","en":"Meditate Naturally is a team installation combining a garment, brainwave data and two projection surfaces to invite attention to the body and nature during meditation. I was responsible for parsing brainwave data, mapping it to TouchDesigner visuals and developing projection feedback across the garment and background."},"question":{"zh":"怎样让身体信号成为可见的图像，让参与者在冥想中重新留意自然？","en":"How can visible responses to bodily signals invite participants to notice nature during meditation?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"以冥想邀请参与","en":"Invite participation through meditation"},"description":{"zh":"团队从城市生活与自然的距离出发，选择安静的身体体验作为参与方式。","en":"The team uses a quiet bodily experience to explore the distance between urban life and nature."}},{"label":{"zh":"设计服装与投影空间","en":"Develop the garment and setting"},"description":{"zh":"团队以 OM 符号发展服装形态，并设置身体与背景两层投影。","en":"The team develops an OM-inspired garment and separate projections on the body and background."}},{"label":{"zh":"将脑波数据映射到视觉","en":"Map brainwave data to visuals"},"description":{"zh":"我解析输入数据，在 TouchDesigner 中建立参数对应，并调试投影反馈。","en":"I parse the incoming data, map it to parameters in TouchDesigner and develop the projection response."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[2],"title":{"zh":"从脑波输入，到身体周围的图像","en":"From brainwave input to a changing projection"},"text":{"zh":"脑波数据经 Arduino 串口进入视觉流程。我负责解析输入，并在 TouchDesigner 中将数值变化对应到自然意象的视觉参数，再输出到服装与背景。花朵、生长和水墨波动等图像，让参与者可以看见信号变化带来的反馈。","en":"Brainwave data enters the visual workflow through an Arduino serial connection. I parse the input, map changing values to nature-inspired parameters in TouchDesigner and send the output to the garment and background. Floral, growth and ink-like imagery makes changes in the signal visible within the installation."},"layout":"immersive","detailsLabel":{"zh":"数据解析、视觉映射与投影反馈说明","en":"Data parsing, visual mapping and projection notes"}},{"sections":[0],"title":{"zh":"用一次安静的体验，谈人与自然的距离","en":"A quiet encounter with the distance from nature"},"text":{"zh":"项目的背景研究涉及濒危物种、城市化与技术依赖。团队选择冥想作为参与方式，希望让观众暂时放慢，通过身体、影像与环境之间的变化接近自然议题。投影反馈因此成为参与过程的一部分，而不只是展示信息的屏幕。","en":"Research into endangered species, urbanisation and technology dependence frames the project. The team chose meditation as a way to slow the encounter, approaching environmental concerns through changes between body, image and surroundings. Projection feedback becomes part of participation rather than simply a screen for information."},"layout":"research","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看自然议题研究与冥想体验的出发点","en":"Read the environmental research and meditation concept"}},{"sections":[1],"title":{"zh":"服装与空间，为投影提供两种表面","en":"A garment and a room as projection surfaces"},"text":{"zh":"团队从 OM 符号发展服装轮廓，并用石头、芦苇和宣纸组织空间。服装与背景形成两层投影，使图像既贴近身体，也延伸到周围环境。我的视觉与投影工作在这一团队设计的场景中呈现。","en":"The team developed the garment silhouette from the OM symbol and arranged the setting with stones, reeds and rice paper. The garment and background provide two projection surfaces, placing imagery close to the body and extending it into the room. My visual and projection work is presented within this team-designed environment."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看团队的服装推演与空间模型","en":"View the team’s garment development and spatial model"}}],"closing":{"zh":"团队完成了服装、空间与交互投影共同组成的装置，我的产出集中在脑波解析、TouchDesigner 映射与反馈呈现。这次实践让我把数据输入、视觉变化与现场投影连成一条完整的制作流程。下一步希望让参与者更容易理解自己的信号与画面变化之间的关系。","en":"The team produced an installation combining garment, space and responsive projection. My contribution connected brainwave parsing, TouchDesigner mapping and projected feedback into one working visual pipeline. Further development would make the relationship between a participant’s signal and the changing imagery easier to understand."}},"moving-crowds":{"subtitle":{"zh":"如果气味也成为一道边界","en":"What if scent became another border?"},"lead":{"zh":"Moving Crowds 设想了一个通过气味识别身份的未来，并以一家虚构生物科技公司回应迁移与身体自主权的问题。项目结合人口流动研究、植物提取与培养皿实验，发展出贴身贴片的产品概念和实验室式展陈。","en":"Moving Crowds imagines a future in which scent identifies people, using a fictional biotech company to question migration and bodily autonomy. Research into population movement, plant-extract experiments and petri-dish observations inform a body-worn patch concept and a laboratory-style installation."},"question":{"zh":"当身体的气味也能被用来识别身份，人们还能如何决定自己去哪里？","en":"If the scent of a body could identify its owner, who would control where that person could go?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"设定气味识别的未来","en":"Imagine scent-based identification"},"description":{"zh":"从迁移限制与身份识别出发，提出 2080 年的假想情境。","en":"Extend research into migration restrictions and identity recognition into a fictional 2080 scenario."}},{"label":{"zh":"用材料实验发展想法","en":"Develop the idea through materials"},"description":{"zh":"记录植物提取、培养皿观察与皮肤附近的材料试验。","en":"Document plant extraction, petri-dish observations and material tests close to the skin."}},{"label":{"zh":"以贴片与公司呈现提案","en":"Present a patch and a company"},"description":{"zh":"通过佩戴草图、产品概念与实验室展陈，讲述未来迁移者的处境。","en":"Use body-placement sketches, a product concept and a laboratory installation to tell the future migrant’s story."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[3],"title":{"zh":"一家为未来迁移者服务的虚构公司","en":"A fictional company for future migrants"},"text":{"zh":"在项目设定的未来，一家生物科技公司提供贴身贴片，声称帮助使用者避开气味识别。产品与实验室式展陈让观众通过熟悉的商业形式，接近一个陌生的问题：当识别深入身体，人们的行动自由会发生什么变化？","en":"Within the project’s imagined future, a biotech company offers a body-worn patch that promises to help users avoid scent-based identification. The product and laboratory-style installation use a familiar commercial format to pose an unfamiliar question: what happens to freedom of movement when identification reaches into the body?"},"layout":"immersive","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看虚构公司的产品叙事与展陈","en":"Explore the fictional company, product story and installation"}},{"sections":[0],"title":{"zh":"从迁移限制，追问身体如何被识别","en":"From restrictions on movement to identifying the body"},"text":{"zh":"人口迁移、限制性政策与劳动力流动构成背景研究。项目将这些议题延伸到 2080 年的假想情境：身份识别不再只依赖证件，身体气味也可能成为边界。贴片因此成为讨论迁移与自主权的设计道具。","en":"Research into migration, restrictive policies and labour movement grounds the project. A fictional 2080 scenario extends these concerns beyond identity documents to the possibility of scent becoming a border. The patch acts as a design prop through which to discuss mobility and autonomy."},"layout":"research","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看迁移研究与 2080 年情境设定","en":"Read the migration research and fictional 2080 scenario"}},{"sections":[1,2],"title":{"zh":"用实验记录与佩戴草图发展贴片","en":"Develop the patch through experiments and body studies"},"text":{"zh":"植物提取、皮肤与汗液采样、培养皿对比为产品概念提供了材料探索。实验日记记录过程，佩戴草图则关注腋下附近的位置、外形与隐藏方式。这些记录把假想服务发展为可以观看和讨论的贴身物件。","en":"Plant extraction, skin and sweat sampling, and petri-dish comparisons provide material exploration for the concept. An experiment diary records the process, while sketches consider placement near the armpit, form and discreet wear. These studies develop the fictional service into a body-worn object that visitors can examine and discuss."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看材料实验日记与贴片佩戴探索","en":"View the material diary and patch-placement studies"}}],"closing":{"zh":"项目形成了推测性贴片、材料实验记录与虚构公司的展陈叙事。它借助贴近身体的物件，讨论人口流动背后较难被看见的识别与控制。未来若继续发展，会更关注迁移者如何理解这家公司的承诺，以及“获得自由”是否又带来新的依赖。","en":"The project produced a speculative patch, material experiment records and an installation built around a fictional company. A body-worn object brings less visible forms of identification and control into a discussion of migration. Further work could explore how migrants understand the company’s promise, and whether buying freedom creates a new dependency."}},"equiflow":{"subtitle":{"zh":"当疗愈开始要求你表现得更好","en":"When healing asks you to perform"},"lead":{"zh":"Equiflow 是一家虚构的数字疗愈公司。我把废墟办公室、VR 绘画和打印证书连接成一段体验：观众先表达情绪，随后发现自己的活动被记录并转成评价。项目借此反思，当疗愈服务以恢复工作状态为目标时，关怀与管理之间的界限在哪里。","en":"Equiflow is a fictional digital-healing company. I connected a ruins-office installation, VR drawing and a printed certificate into an experience in which visitors express their emotions, then discover that their activity has been recorded and assessed. The project questions the boundary between care and management when healing is framed as a return to productivity."},"question":{"zh":"当疗愈开始记录情绪、奖励参与并评价表现，谁来决定一个人是否“已经疗愈”？","en":"When healing records emotions, rewards participation and evaluates performance, who decides whether someone has been healed?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"选择情绪","en":"Choose an emotion"},"description":{"zh":"用预设情绪和路径提示，把个人感受带入系统的分类。","en":"Predefined emotions and route prompts bring personal feelings into the system’s categories."}},{"label":{"zh":"记录表达","en":"Record expression"},"description":{"zh":"让自由绘画进入持续参与的流程，并留下轨迹与停顿记录。","en":"Spatial drawing becomes part of an engagement loop, leaving traces and pauses for the system to read."}},{"label":{"zh":"生成证书","en":"Issue a certificate"},"description":{"zh":"用分析反馈和完成奖励，把表达转为一份可被评价的记录。","en":"Analytical feedback and a completion reward turn expression into an assessable record."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[5,6,9],"title":{"zh":"从废墟办公室进入 VR","en":"From the office into VR"},"text":{"zh":"实体装置先呈现职场压力，再邀请观众戴上头显、选择情绪并开始绘画。空间中的破损办公物件与温和的引导形成反差，为最后的证书评价建立语境。","en":"The installation makes workplace pressure visible before inviting visitors to put on a headset, choose an emotion and draw. Broken office objects contrast with gentle instructions, setting up the assessment that arrives with the certificate."},"layout":"immersive","detailsLabel":{"zh":"装置入口与 VR 绘画流程说明","en":"Installation entry and VR drawing-flow notes"}},{"sections":[1,2],"title":{"zh":"研究数字疗愈的参与机制","en":"Study how digital healing guides participation"},"text":{"zh":"我以 Headspace、Calm 和 Lyra 为研究案例，整理情绪标签、持续使用激励和企业心理健康服务中的数据关系。这些观察成为情绪入口、奖励反馈和证书评价的设计依据。","en":"Research into Headspace, Calm and Lyra focused on emotion labels, incentives for continued use and data relationships in employer-led mental-health services. These observations informed the emotion entry, reward feedback and certificate assessment."},"layout":"research","detailsLabel":{"zh":"参考案例与体验机制的对应关系","en":"How the research references inform the experience"}},{"sections":[3,4],"title":{"zh":"把关怀写成系统规则","en":"Turn an offer of care into rules"},"text":{"zh":"系统先让观众选择如何描述自己，再通过提示和奖励推动体验继续，最后用证书总结表现。我把这三个环节放在同一流程中，追问谁有权定义“已经疗愈”。","en":"The system first asks visitors to describe themselves, then uses prompts and rewards to sustain participation, and finally summarizes their performance in a certificate. Bringing these steps together asks who gets to decide that someone has been healed."},"layout":"mechanisms","detailsLabel":{"zh":"情绪选项、奖励与评价规则","en":"Emotion choices, rewards and assessment rules"}},{"sections":[7,8],"title":{"zh":"从绘画记录到打印证书","en":"From drawing traces to a printed certificate"},"text":{"zh":"旅程图梳理情绪选择、VR 绘画、活动记录、AI 辅助反馈与证书输出的先后关系。技术流程把输入、处理和输出并列呈现，让观众看见私人表达如何进入系统的评价标准。","en":"The journey map connects emotion selection, VR drawing, activity records, AI-assisted feedback and certificate output. Mapping the input, processing and output reveals how a private act of expression enters the system’s criteria for assessment."},"layout":"sequence","detailsLabel":{"zh":"活动记录、反馈与证书输出说明","en":"Activity records, feedback and certificate-output notes"}}],"closing":{"zh":"项目形成了废墟办公室展陈、VR 绘画原型，以及从情绪入口到证书输出的完整体验叙事。后续重点是结合观众访谈，检查他们在何时察觉评价与控制，并据此调整引导、奖励和证书的呈现节奏。","en":"The project brings together a ruins-office installation, a VR drawing prototype and an experience narrative from emotion selection to certificate output. The next focus is visitor interviews: when do people notice assessment and control, and how should that inform the timing of prompts, rewards and the certificate?"}},"clink":{"subtitle":{"zh":"把监测、问诊与用药接成一条服务流程","en":"Connect monitoring, consultation and medication"},"lead":{"zh":"外婆的二型糖尿病照护经历，让我关注老年患者在监测、就诊和用药之间反复衔接的困难。我通过患者、家属和医生访谈梳理需求，并将服务蓝图转为医疗车与 App 方案。","en":"My grandmother’s experience of type 2 diabetes drew my attention to the handoffs older patients face between monitoring, appointments and medication. Interviews with patients, families and doctors informed a service blueprint, medical-cart concept and app interfaces."},"question":{"zh":"如何让老年糖尿病患者的监测、问诊与用药形成一条清楚、连贯的服务流程？","en":"How can monitoring, consultation and medication form a clear, connected service for older people with diabetes?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"了解日常困难","en":"Understand daily difficulties"},"description":{"zh":"从家庭照护经历出发，梳理监测、用药与就诊中的具体问题。","en":"Start with a family care experience and examine practical problems across monitoring, medication and appointments."}},{"label":{"zh":"梳理服务分工","en":"Map service responsibilities"},"description":{"zh":"结合多方访谈，在服务蓝图中连接患者、家属、社区和医院。","en":"Use interviews to connect patients, families, community care and hospitals in a service blueprint."}},{"label":{"zh":"落实服务触点","en":"Design the touchpoints"},"description":{"zh":"将远程咨询、检测和用药支持落实到医疗车与 App 界面。","en":"Translate consultation, testing and medication support into medical-cart and app interactions."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[0,1],"title":{"zh":"从患者、家属和医生了解需求","en":"Understand patients, families and clinicians"},"text":{"zh":"我从家庭经历展开医疗服务研究，并访谈患者、家属、社区医生和中心医院医生。整理结果聚焦四类困难：理解治疗信息、完成操作、安排照护和衔接就诊。","en":"I expanded a family experience into service research and interviews with patients, relatives, community doctors and central-hospital doctors. The synthesis focuses on four difficulties: understanding treatment information, completing tasks, coordinating care and arranging appointments."},"layout":"research","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看访谈整理与用户画像","en":"View interview synthesis and personas"}},{"sections":[2],"title":{"zh":"用服务蓝图明确各方分工","en":"Clarify responsibilities in the blueprint"},"text":{"zh":"服务蓝图把患者、家属、社区医院、中心医院和药房放在同一条流程中，梳理监测、远程咨询与药品支持的衔接。实体服务与数字信息因此有了共同的流程依据。","en":"The service blueprint places patients, families, community hospitals, central hospitals and pharmacies in one flow. It maps the handoffs for monitoring, remote consultation and medication support, giving physical services and digital information a shared structure."},"layout":"system","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看服务地图与触点衔接","en":"View the service map and touchpoint handoffs"}},{"sections":[3],"title":{"zh":"将服务落到医疗车与 App","en":"Translate the service into cart and app"},"text":{"zh":"医疗车承接检测与服务接触，App 承接问诊和用药相关的信息与操作。我将两者与服务蓝图对应，展示患者如何在实体和数字触点之间继续完成任务。","en":"The medical-cart concept provides a physical point for testing and care, while the app organizes information and actions for consultation and medication. Both are mapped back to the blueprint to show how patients move between physical and digital touchpoints."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"医疗车与患者端界面的设计说明","en":"Mobile-clinic and patient-interface design notes"}}],"closing":{"zh":"CLINK 形成了访谈与用户画像、服务地图、服务蓝图，以及医疗车和患者端 App 方案。后续重点是让老年患者和医护人员走查典型任务，检查操作提示是否容易理解、服务交接是否清楚。","en":"CLINK brings together interview findings, personas, a service map and blueprint, and medical-cart and patient-app designs. The next focus is walking through typical tasks with older patients and clinicians to examine instructions and service handoffs."}},"five-stars":{"subtitle":{"zh":"让家长清楚地找到、比较并联系老师","en":"Help parents find, compare and contact tutors"},"lead":{"zh":"这个网站设计面向寻找辅导资源的学生和家长。我围绕学科查找、教师信息比较、注册与顾问咨询组织页面，并为教师设置独立的入驻路径，让两类用户各自找到下一步。","en":"This website design is for students and parents looking for tutoring support. I organized the pages around subject search, tutor comparison, registration and consultant advice, with a separate onboarding route for teachers so each group has a clear next step."},"question":{"zh":"家长在联系老师前，怎样快速了解学科匹配、资质、费用和可预约时间？","en":"How can parents understand subject fit, credentials, price and availability before contacting a tutor?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"明确首页入口","en":"Clarify the entry points"},"description":{"zh":"在首页区分找老师、看学科和咨询三种任务。","en":"Separate finding a tutor, exploring subjects and seeking advice on the homepage."}},{"label":{"zh":"组织比较信息","en":"Organize comparison information"},"description":{"zh":"把学科、认证、评分、价格和可用时间放入浏览路径。","en":"Bring subjects, certification, ratings, prices and availability into the browsing flow."}},{"label":{"zh":"区分注册路径","en":"Separate registration routes"},"description":{"zh":"让学生和家长选择注册或咨询，为教师提供独立入驻入口。","en":"Offer registration or consultation to students and parents, with a separate entry for teachers."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[0],"title":{"zh":"首页先回答“从哪里开始”","en":"Show visitors where to start"},"text":{"zh":"首页先介绍辅导服务，再把浏览老师、探索学科和顾问咨询放在明确的位置。每个入口对应一项用户任务，访客可以按自己已知的信息选择起点。","en":"The homepage introduces the tutoring service and gives clear places to browse tutors, explore subjects or contact a consultant. Each entry corresponds to a task, so visitors can start with the information they already have."},"layout":"overview","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看首页信息层级与任务入口","en":"View homepage hierarchy and task entry points"}},{"sections":[1],"title":{"zh":"找老师时就能比较关键信息","en":"Compare key information while browsing tutors"},"text":{"zh":"搜索围绕老师姓名和学科展开，浏览信息进一步呈现认证、评分、价格与可用时间。我把查找和比较放在连续的路径中，让联系前的判断有据可依。","en":"Search is organized around tutor names and subjects; browsing adds certification, ratings, prices and availability. The design connects discovery and comparison so that visitors have useful information before deciding to make contact."},"layout":"comparison","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看老师信息、搜索与比较结构","en":"View tutor information, search and comparison"}},{"sections":[2],"title":{"zh":"学生注册与教师入驻分开","en":"Separate student registration and teacher onboarding"},"text":{"zh":"学生和家长可以继续注册，也可以通过顾问咨询获得学习建议；教师则从独立入口申请入驻。不同身份的路径在桌面和移动页面中保持清楚。","en":"Students and parents can register or seek learning advice through a consultant, while teachers use a dedicated entry to join the platform. These distinct routes remain clear across desktop and mobile layouts."},"layout":"sequence","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看学生注册、咨询与教师入驻路径","en":"View registration, consultation and teacher entry routes"}}],"closing":{"zh":"项目形成了首页、教师查找与比较、学生注册和顾问咨询的响应式网站设计。我把找老师与教师入驻分开处理，让服务介绍、选择依据和后续行动出现在清楚的浏览路径中。设计重点是帮助不同身份的用户理解各自的选择，并清楚下一步可以做什么。","en":"The project produced responsive designs for the homepage, tutor discovery and comparison, student registration and consultant support. Separating tutor discovery from teacher onboarding gave service information, comparison criteria and actions a clear place in each journey. The design focuses on helping different users understand their next step."}},"rako-rako-ramen":{"subtitle":{"zh":"让品牌印象顺畅衔接到商品选择","en":"Connect the brand experience to product choice"},"lead":{"zh":"Rako Rako Ramen 是一个英国拉面品牌的商业网站设计项目。我负责 UX/UI、商品目录结构和品牌叙事，将口味、份量、价格与库存信息组织为单品和套装页面，并交付网站设计方案。","en":"Rako Rako Ramen is a commercial website design project for a UK ramen brand. I was responsible for UX/UI, product-catalog structure and brand storytelling, delivering designs that organize flavour, quantity, price and availability across individual products and bundles."},"question":{"zh":"怎样在保持品牌个性的同时，让访客清楚比较口味、份量、价格和库存状态？","en":"How can the store retain its character while making flavours, quantities, prices and availability easy to compare?"},"steps":[{"label":{"zh":"建立品牌印象","en":"Introduce the brand"},"description":{"zh":"用拉面图像和产品命名呈现品牌，让商品入口紧接视觉内容。","en":"Use ramen imagery and product naming to introduce the brand, with product entries close to the visuals."}},{"label":{"zh":"说明单品差异","en":"Explain product differences"},"description":{"zh":"统一呈现口味、价格和库存状态，便于比较核心单品。","en":"Present flavour, price and stock status consistently across the core products."}},{"label":{"zh":"按场景组织套装","en":"Group bundles by occasion"},"description":{"zh":"用尝鲜、宵夜和囤货等套餐承接不同数量与场景需求。","en":"Use sampling, late-night and freezer-stock bundles for different occasions and quantities."}}],"chapters":[{"sections":[0],"title":{"zh":"品牌首页直接连接商品","en":"Connect the brand homepage to products"},"text":{"zh":"首页通过拉面图像、视觉识别和产品命名建立品牌印象，同时把商品卡片和购买入口放在浏览路径中。访客看完品牌内容后，可以继续选择具体商品。","en":"The homepage establishes the brand through ramen imagery, visual identity and product naming, while keeping product cards and purchase actions within the browsing flow. Visitors can move from the brand introduction to a specific product."},"layout":"immersive","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看品牌首页与商品入口安排","en":"View the brand homepage and product entry points"}},{"sections":[1],"title":{"zh":"用一致的信息比较三种口味","en":"Compare three flavours with consistent information"},"text":{"zh":"经典豚骨、香辣豚骨和黑蒜豚骨是目录中的核心单品。我用一致的图片、命名、价格和库存状态组织商品卡片，让风味差异与购买信息同时可见。","en":"Classic tonkotsu, spicy tonkotsu and black garlic tonkotsu form the core range. Consistent product images, names, prices and stock status keep flavour differences and practical purchase information together."},"layout":"comparison","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看口味分类与商品卡片信息","en":"View flavour categories and product-card information"}},{"sections":[2],"title":{"zh":"按尝鲜、宵夜与囤货选择套装","en":"Choose bundles for sampling, late nights or stocking up"},"text":{"zh":"Ramen Sampler Box、Late-Night Survival Kit 和 Freezer Stock Box 分别对应尝鲜、即时用餐和囤货需求。套装让用户除口味之外，还能按数量和食用场景作选择。","en":"The Ramen Sampler Box, Late-Night Survival Kit and Freezer Stock Box address sampling, an immediate meal and stocking up. Bundles add quantity and occasion as ways to choose alongside flavour."},"layout":"paired","detailsLabel":{"zh":"查看三类套装与选择路径","en":"View the three bundle types and selection routes"}}],"closing":{"zh":"项目交付了品牌首页、单品目录和场景套装的页面设计。我的重点是在保留品牌辨识度的同时，用一致的口味、份量、价格与库存信息支持商品比较，并让套装回应尝鲜、宵夜和囤货等具体需求。","en":"The design delivery covers the brand homepage, individual-product catalog and occasion-based bundles. My focus was to retain the brand’s character while using consistent flavour, quantity, price and stock information to support comparison. Bundles respond to concrete needs such as sampling, late-night meals and stocking the freezer."}}};
